course: dictionary
lesson: 1310
title: A prickly word from the desert
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cactus is a plant that grows in hot, dry places such as deserts. Its thick stem stores water, so it can survive when rain is rare. Most cacti have spines instead of leaves, which protect them and lose less water.
explain: Use the context to check your idea. «Nature is lovely to look at but not always to touch: lambs in spring fields, blackberries on a hedge, cacti in the desert and fire ant nests all need care.» The clue is "not always to touch" and "need care", so a cactus must be something that can hurt you when you touch it.
explain: Cactus has a plural too. One cactus, many cacti (or cactuses). Test it by swapping your meaning into the sentence: "The desert is full of plants with thick stems that store water" fits, so you have understood the word.
fact: A cactus is a plant that grows in hot, dry places such as deserts.
fact: Cacti store water in their thick stems, so they can live where rain is rare.
fact: Most cacti have spines instead of leaves, because spines lose less water.
fact: «Cactus» has the plural «cacti», and «cactuses» is also correct.
fact: The elf owl nests in old woodpecker holes in «saguaro cactuses» and eats moths, crickets and even scorpions.
exercise: «The desert was full of tall cacti with sharp spines.» What is a cactus? | *A plant with a thick stem that stores water | A cold, wet bog plant | A rock that holds sand | A small desert animal that eats seeds
exercise: Why do cacti have spines instead of leaves? | To catch rain from the clouds | To help them float on sand | *To protect the plant and lose less water | To make them smell sweet
exercise: Find and copy the plural of cactus in this sentence: «The hot desert is full of cacti.» | *cacti | hot | full | desert
test: «Many cacti grow in the desert, and their thick stems store water.» Why can a cactus live in the desert? | It only needs water once a year from a river | It hides under the sand all day | It has big, wide leaves that catch the sun | *Its thick stem stores water when rain is rare
test: The Galápagos tortoise can stretch up to «tall cactus» to eat. What does this tell you about cactus? | It is always underwater | *It can grow tall enough for a tortoise to reach | It is an animal that eats tortoises | It is a kind of sand
exam: «The red food colour carmine is made from crushed cochineal bugs that live on cactus.» What is a cactus in this sentence? | A sweet that is coloured red | A kind of lipstick | A type of bug | *A plant that the cochineal bugs live on
